course: dictionary
lesson: 5650
title: Lipstick: colour, stick and clue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lipstick is a colour for the lips. It usually comes as a small stick that slides out of a tube, so a lipstick can mean the stick or tube itself. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits. «Mum put on red lipstick before the party.» Here, put on tells you the colour went onto her lips.
explain: Lipstick can be a clue. «The detective found a lipstick message written on the mirror.» A message written in lipstick is an unusual thing to find, so it could help solve the mystery. Ask yourself what the words around it suggest, then check your meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Lipstick is also part of a famous phrase. «Lipstick on a pig» means making something bad look better on the outside only, and the bad thing is still there underneath. Phrases like this often do not mean what the words say, so context matters.
explain: Lipstick is not only for make-up. «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs that live on cactus, and it is used in sweets, yoghurt and lipstick; the Aztecs used it to dye cloth.» Here lipstick is a place where a colour is used, and it shows how one colour can appear in very different things.
fact: Lipstick means colour for the lips, usually in a small stick that comes out of a tube.
fact: A lipstick can also mean the stick or tube of this colour, so one lipstick is one stick.
fact: Lipstick is uncountable when you mean the colour in general: some lipstick, not some lipsticks.
fact: «Lipstick on a pig» means making something bad look better on the outside only.
fact: In science, lipstick can be tested for its colours using chromatography, which separates a colour into the different colours it is made from.
exercise: «She wiped the red lipstick off her lips before school.» What is lipstick here? | A small brush for painting walls | *A colour for the lips, usually in a small stick | A kind of hat worn in the rain | A cold drink with cherry flavour
exercise: «The detective found a lipstick message written on the mirror.» What could this message be in a story? | A recipe for a cake | A new kind of window | A reflection of the sun | *A clue that may help solve the mystery
exercise: What does the phrase «lipstick on a pig» mean? | *Making something bad look better on the outside only | A pig that has been painted for a show | Feeding a pig sweets and cake | A pig that wins a prize at the fair
test: «Mia bought a new tube of red lipstick.» What does the word tube show about lipstick? | *That lipstick can come in a tube | That lipstick is always a liquid | That lipstick is only for children | That lipstick is a food
test: Which word is the plural of lipstick? | lipstickes | lipstickies | *lipsticks | lipstick's
exam: Which science test can separate the colours in lipstick? | *Chromatography | Multiplication | Photosynthesis | Gravity
